<title>USA: Louisiana Land files shelf for $500 million.</title>
<headline>Louisiana Land files shelf for $500 million.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS, La. 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Louisiana Land and Exploration Co said Friday it has filed a shelf registration statement to issue up to $500 million of securities.</p>
<p>The company said the registration replaces the undrawn balance of the shelf registration it filed in 1993.</p>
<p>The company said it sees no need to issue either debt or equity securities under the shelf in the near future. The purpose of the shelf &quot;is to simply increase the company's flexibility to opportunistically finance future growth,&quot; it said.</p>
</text>
